From 81b873bcaab7a0647bd6af72572511e6e883c91d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 04:43:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat: POWERINFER_IOCP runtime toggle for the Windows
 expert-read path

Charter ask #3 ("certain options that can be turned on/off, documented as
well" -> "All options compiled in, runtime-toggled"): the M2b IOCP port was
compile-time unconditional on every Windows build, with no way to fall back
without a recompile. Sol's audit rated IOCP high-risk, so the previous
synchronous path is PRESERVED as the OFF branch, not deleted.

POWERINFER_IOCP defaults ON; only an exact "0" selects the pre-M2b synchronous
ReadFile+OVERLAPPED path. The env is read once into a function-local static,
matching the lane110_prof_enabled() idiom in ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ops.cpp (exact
single-character parse, no per-call getenv).

Mechanics:
- iou.cpp: FILE_FLAG_OVERLAPPED and the completion port are created only in
  IOCP mode; enqueue_read takes a synchronous branch that completes in place
  and queues the completion; submit_and_wait is a no-op when OFF. reap() is
  shared by both modes - both push a RequestData slot and a byte count, so
  slot release and exactly-once semantics are identical either way.
- expert_cache.cpp: the IOCP worker loop is now guarded by iocp_enabled() and
  returns; when OFF, control falls through to the original loop, which is the
  SAME loop Linux uses. Pre-M2b Windows behavior is therefore restored exactly,
  not re-implemented.

Linux io_uring remains untouched and unconditional.

OPTIONS-REGISTRY row added. Cost ON and OFF are both recorded UNMEASURED:
the single IOCP arm measured so far is confounded (sub-floor RAM, non-isolated
HEAD), and Sol's "10-40% cold-regime" figure is an audit ESTIMATE, cited as
such, never measured on this box.

Ported-mechanism: compile-time #if branch -> runtime env toggle, sync path retained
Source-path: powerinfer/moe_sparse_pipeline/{iou.cpp,iou.hpp,expert_cache.cpp}, docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md
Evidence: research/local-inference/trials/2026-07-22-arifilabs-combined-fork-charter.md
Origin: ArifiLabs/iocp-async
